31152      title 'Semivariogram Model Fitting of Log-Arsenic Concentration';
31153      data logAsData;
31154      input East North logAs @@;
31155      label logAs='log(As) Concentration';
31156      datalines;

NOTE: SAS went to a new line when INPUT statement reached past the end of a line.
NOTE: The data set WORK.LOGASDATA has 138 observations and 3 variables.

31203      ;
31204      ods graphics on;
31205      proc variogram data=logAsData plots=pairs(mid);
31206      compute novariogram nhc=50;
31207      coord xc=East yc=North;
31208      var logAs;
31209      run;

NOTE: The PROCEDURE VARIOGRAM printed page 1978.

31210      proc variogram data=logAsData plots(only)=semivar;
31211      compute lagd=5 maxlag=40;
31212      coord xc=East yc=North;
31213      var logAs;
31214      run;

NOTE: No DIRECTIONS statement and no NDIRECTIONS=, or NDIRECTIONS=0 specified: Computing omnidirectional semivariogram.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE VARIOGRAM printed pages 1979-1980.

31215      proc variogram data=logAsData plots(only)=fit;
31216      store out=SemivAsStore / label='LogAs Concentration Models';
31217      compute lagd=5 maxlag=40;
31218      coord xc=East yc=North;
31219      model form=auto(mlist=(exp,gau,mat) nest=1 to 2);
31220      var logAs;
31221      run;

NOTE: No DIRECTIONS statement and no NDIRECTIONS=, or NDIRECTIONS=0 specified: Computing omnidirectional semivariogram.
NOTE: Matern form replaced with Gaussian form in one or more models because the smoothing parameter exceeded the MTOGTOL= option threshold. This action 
      resulted in 1 duplicate model(s) whose re-fitting was skipped.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE VARIOGRAM printed pages 1981-1983.

31222      ods graphics off;
31223      run;
31224      quit;
